From c32a71bb730e697868f56b3caeea64706dae4a7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:59:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] DUALCOIL9050: HT9050 five-port three-position cylinders --
 Pop / Off energise "<name>Off", Push / On release it -- EastSun 1008
 'Cylinder[C_LoaderEdgePush].Pop() == Cylinder[C_LoaderEdgePush].Off() &&
 Cylinder[C_LoaderEdgePushOff].On(), Push() the reverse'.

mycylin.cpp: TMyCylinder::OnSwitch (On / Push output) calls g_W906PairedCoilHook(name, false) first, OffSwitch (Off / Pop output)
  calls g_W906PairedCoilHook(name, true) last (same lines); the pointer is defined at the end of the file, 0 by default, so test
  targets that compile mycylin.cpp alone (GA1_cprod) and other machines stay golden.
JsonBridge/W906DualCoil9050.cpp (new, compiled into wb_serve directly, static registrar): only HT9050, only when the "<name>Off"
  IO_Table row exists, is IOType Cylinder and Enable=1, and is not itself an engine Cylinder[] (golden C_DockXAxisOff style).
  Writes the row with the io.btnPanelClick OutType rule, local iterator (not HSys.mapIOTableIter). The machine table has 27 pairs.
  The IO page's manual click is unchanged (golden single-point write).
JsonBridge/IoBtnPanelClick.cpp UPCYLOFF: the Off coil is held like every Pop, no longer released after 500 ms (same lines).
tests: new test_dualcoil9050.cpp (HT9050_DualCoil 26/26: both coils for Pop / Push / On / Off, off-before-on order, non-HT9050
  untouched, Enable=0 / non-Cylinder row / engine-owned name untouched, disabled cylinder untouched). W6_1_EmptyCanary, W6_Canary,
  GA1_cprod passed. Release linked; Debug compiled (link waits for wb_serve to close).
Backups D:\HT9045\_review\*.bak_dualcoil9050_20261008_015205. WORKLOG row 199.

